  "passages": [
    {
      "id": "b1.work-and-careers.first-real-job",
      "level": "B1",
      "topics": ["work-and-careers"],
      "title": "My first real job",
      "text": "Carlos has worked at a small design company in Monterrey for two years. Before that, he applied for more than twenty jobs, and most companies turned him down because he didn't have enough experience. Finally, a manager invited him to an interview and offered him a position the same week. The salary was not very high, but the work was interesting. At his company, everyone has to arrive by nine, but employees don't have to wear a suit. They must not use their phones during meetings, though. Carlos gets along well with his colleagues, and they often have lunch together. The hardest part of the job is the deadlines: sometimes he has to work late to finish a project on time. Last month he got promoted to team leader, so now he has more responsibility and a better salary. A bigger company has offered him a job, but he has decided to stay. \"I've learned so much here,\" he says. \"I'm not ready to quit.\"",
      "source": {
        "kind": "original"
      }
    }
  ],
